    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are prioritizing speed-conducive matchups today, headlined by **Trea Turner** (77.33), who remains our most explosive play. Facing Dollander, **Trea Turner** benefits significantly from a slow pitcher delivery window, making him a prime candidate to capitalize on our league\u2019s aggressive stolen base weighting. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.93) is a high-upside play despite his #8 batting position; the matchup against Rocker offers a massive 14% platoon edge and, like **Trea Turner**, he faces a pitcher susceptible to the stolen base, pushing him well above his raw projection. **Kyle Schwarber** (70.60) completes our top-tier tier, as his elite xwOBA (0.394) paired with the favorable #2 spot in the order provides a high-floor contribution for both R and HR categories.\n\nWhile **Carson Benge** (59.99) nearly breached the elite threshold, the most difficult decision involved **Yordan Alvarez** (54.97) and **Dillon Dingler** (56.05). **Yordan Alvarez** remains a start despite the disadvantageous L/L matchup against Lodolo, as his elite power profile (0.425 xwOBA) provides a ceiling that few on our bench can match. **Colt Keith** was the primary candidate to displace the bottom of our lineup, but he remains benched as he is currently out of the starting rotation. We are monitoring **Dillon Dingler** closely; while his 56.05 score is bolstered by a strong platoon advantage against Bubic, he is currently living on the margin of our efficiency targets. \n\nRisk management for the Zebras remains focused on SP skill levels. We are bracing for potential regression against pitchers like Detmers, who poses a significant threat to **Kazuma Okamoto** (47.46) and **Caleb Durbin** (40.89). Both players suffer from a 19% SP skill penalty, placing them in the marginal category. We will rely on the high-speed utility of our middle-of-the-pack players like **Luke Raley** (55.03) to stabilize our SB totals while waiting for our primary power bats to break through the tough opposing ERAs. Bench stalwarts like **Christian Yelich**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** are unavailable or currently held in reserve to maintain roster flexibility as we navigate the upcoming series.",
